Example 8.18: In a capacitor of capacitance 20 \mu F, the distance between the plates is 2 \mu F, the dielectric slab of width 1 mm and dielectric constant 2 is inserted between the plates, what is the new capacitance?
Solution: Given
C = 20 \ \mu\text{F} = 20 \times 10^{-6} \,\text{F}
d = 2 \ \text{mm} = 2 \times 10^{-3} \,\text{m}
t = 1 \times 10^{-3} \,\text{m}
k = 2
C = \frac{A\varepsilon_0}{d} \text{ and } C' = \frac{A\varepsilon_0}{d - t + \frac{t}{k}}
\Rightarrow \frac{C}{C'} = \frac{d - t + \frac{t}{k}}{d}
\Rightarrow \frac{20}{C'} = \frac{\left(2 \times 10^{-3} - 1 \times 10^{-3} + \frac{1 \times 10^{-3}}{2}\right)}{2 \times 10^{-3}}
\Rightarrow C' = 26.67 \ \mu\text{F}
